```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: WASI runtime users (ROS 2 robotics via Eclipse Foundation default transport, knqyf263/go-plugin generator users, dylibso/observe-sdk users) who run WASM guests that rely on WASI random_get for cryptographic secrets (ed25519 key generation, getrandom, crypto/rand) and expect the host to honor the WASI CSPRNG contract. The guest cannot defend itself because preview1 ABI has exactly one randomness function (random_get, returns only errno) with no entropy-quality query, CSPRNG capability assertion, or self-test (L2 GUEST-DEFENSIBILITY).
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Real win, not microbenchmark-only. L0 EXP-0083 demonstrates 30/30 cross-process byte-identical ed25519 keys under default and 10/10 cross-language Rust getrandom identical outputs, with clock-decoupling ~31x. L2 GUEST-DEFENSIBILITY confirms crypto/rand.Read returns n=32 err=nil with keys byte-identical across restarts, invisible to correct guest code. L2 VERSION TRAJECTORY shows v1.12.0 (2026-05-28) latest tag still ships const seed=int64(42) with default wiring. L2 NODE.js/V8 BASELINE establishes wazero as sole anomaly vs Wasmtime (ChaCha CSPRNG), Wasmer (OS getrandom), Node/V8 (uvwasi secure). This is a security correctness failure producing globally predictable secrets, not a performance artifact.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Practitioner prior art] CrowdSec PR#4495, wetware#106, wapc-go, wazero#620 independently found+fixed this exact composition (L2 CONTRIBUTION POSITIONED), narrowing novelty and indicating insiders already mitigated. [Bounded prevalence] Auth-blocked scan (no GH token) yields n=9 bounded sample: 2 real unmitigated bare-default exposures (knqyf263/go-plugin generator-propagated via gen/host.go:145 into every generated host = blast-radius amplifier; dylibso/observe-sdk loads arbitrary user WASM bare) and 2 explicit overrides (wapc-go, loopholelabs/scale) (L2 PREVALENCE). No population estimate, no evidence of widespread ROS 2 crypto usage via wazero. [Spec contestability] Successor spec violation is unambiguous (cryptographically secure + must be unpredictable + deterministic envs must OMIT); preview1 breach is strong-but-contestable (blocking clause + reference impl behavior vs literal "high-quality" text, fixed-seed never blocks) (L2 SPEC DISAMBIGUATION). [Trivial host fix] Host-side mitigation is low-friction (provide OS CSPRNG), but default remains insecure and invisible to guests.
RATIONALE: L0 EXP-0083 (30/30 identical keys, cross-language ABI-boundary, source-verified defaults); L2 GUEST-DEFENSIBILITY (no guest-side defense possible, entire preview1 ABI has exactly one randomness function); L2 NODE.js/V8 BASELINE (wazero sole anomaly across 4 major runtimes); L2 VERSION TRAJECTORY (v1.12.0 latest, seed=42 persists); L2 PREVALENCE (bounded n=9, 2 unmitigated + generator amplifier, auth-blocked, not population estimate); L2 CONTRIBUTION POSITIONED (practitioners already found+fixed piecemeal, synthesis validates hazard but narrows novelty); L2 SPEC DISAMBIGUATION (successor unambiguous, preview1 strong-but-contestable). Real use case and operational significance are confirmed (predictable secrets in production), but prevalence is bounded-signal with practitioner prior art already addressing known instances; the synthesis does not demonstrate population-scale unmitigated exposure. Honest YELLOW.
```
